    "expectedRule": "Chapter 16 escorts a survivor whose HP runs 0-100 from 100. The first clear of a monster costs it 10 and of a trap 15 (no rescue_carbine, evacuation_plate or qin_che here). The first clear of a checkpoint (north, central, south) leaves a pending checkpoint that blocks leaving with `护送检查点尚未处理，请先选择救治或强推。`; law/resolve-escort-checkpoint treats for one healing pill available on both the run and hub tracks (+25, clamped at 100; refused at full HP) or pushes (-10 and 200 run reward points); a refused choice changes nothing. shelter_gate and south_checkpoint each give one healing pill to both tracks, and every third cleared node adds an exploration supply item in the rotation healing pill, armor patch, focus incense, so south_checkpoint (the third clear after shelter_gate and alarm_grid_trap) adds a second pill: 1 + 2 - 1 treated = 2 left. Display: title 失联护送律; severity resolved once all three checkpoints are resolved or frozen, otherwise danger while pending or at HP <= 40, warning at <= 74, stable above; meter {HP, 100}; targetReached when all are resolved and nothing is pending. Gates: shelter_evacuation_cache_* need all checkpoints and HP >= 75 (`完成三处检查点且幸存者HP至少75。`), shelter_memory_boss_gate (survivor_memory_stage -> shelter_overseer) all checkpoints (`完成三处护送检查点后开放。`). Selecting the boss freezes bossSurvivorSnapshot = HP (no blackbox_beacon); in the boss encounter HP >= 75 gives enemy all stats -6% and outgoing force/art +6%. The pursuer is a separate run system and is disabled after entry so it cannot ambush the walk. All expected values are frozen here, never read from candidate code."
  },
